# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT WORK HERE, AND WHY THIS FILE IS NEARLY EMPTY
#
# This file used to carry rules like:
#
#     /data/trivia-library.json    /404  404
#
# meaning "serve a 404 for the question bank". It never worked. Cloudflare Pages
# supports 200 (rewrite) and the redirect statuses (301/302/303/307/308) in
# _redirects; a bare 404 status is not honoured, so the rule was silently
# ignored and the whole 41,000-question bank was downloadable by anyone who
# guessed the URL, for as long as that rule had been sitting here looking like
# protection. Verified against production on 18 Aug 2026: the URL returned 200.
#
# A file that IS in the deployed directory will be served. So the only reliable
# way to keep something off the public site is to keep it out of the directory
# Pages deploys.
#
# That is why the schema, both Workers, the seed and maintenance scripts and the
# bulk data files now live in ../venueplay-backend/, a sibling of this folder and
# therefore outside this Pages project. The layout there mirrors this one, so the
# scripts' data paths still resolve.
#
# venueplay/data/ keeps only the files the site actually fetches at runtime:
# musical-library.json, trivia-count.json, music-count.json and (2 Nov 2026)
# live-here-now.json, the coaster page's 120 NO-BOARD questions, public on purpose: a
# round played on the phone with no board has to hand the phone its questions. Since
# 21 Nov 2026 the board questions and their answers are only in the game Worker.
#
# If you add anything private in future: put it in venueplay-backend/, not here,
# and do not rely on a rule in this file to hide it.

# ONE OFFER PAGE, A MONTH AT A TIME (Dean, 25 Sep 2026). /offer-<month> is served from the /nsw
# page, which reads the month from the address and shows that month's closing date and code.
# 200 = a rewrite: the visitor keeps the address. A new month is a new line here and a new row
# in nsw.html OFFERS. Plain /offer is NOT an offer: it goes to the homepage and the $3 rate.
# The short sign-in link in a text (Dean, 6 Nov 2026): venueplay.com.au/s/AB12CD7K is served by s.html, which
# moves the code into /app/go's fragment. Our own domain, never a third-party shortener.
/s/*  /s  200
# The code on a printed musical bingo card (13 Nov 2026): /c/<21 characters> is served by c.html, which asks the game Worker whose card it
# is and sends a player's phone to that venue's join page. A code that does not check out lands on the 404 page, as before.
/c/*  /c  200
# The easy way back in by the venue's (public) code: /go/ABC123 opens go-venue.html, which only offers to send a
# sign-in link to whatever is on that account. The code is never a login key on its own.
/go/*  /go-venue  200
/offer-oct  /nsw  200
/offer-nov  /nsw  200
/offer-dec  /nsw  200
/offer-jan  /nsw  200
# /offer-dec-countdown: the December countdown emails (Dean, 22 Nov 2026); its last day is DEC_COUNTDOWN_ENDS in /app/vp-offer.js.
# NO comment after a rule on the same line: Cloudflare Pages drops the whole rule (live /quick/:code was a 404 for that, 22 Nov 2026).
/offer-dec-countdown  /nsw  200
/offer-feb  /nsw  200
/offer-mar  /nsw  200
/offer      /     302
# JOURNEY TRACKING (INBOX 413): a tracked email link is the page's own address plus a short code, venueplay.com.au/offer-nov/MPYXPG.
# The page is served as is (200 rewrite, the address stays); /app/vp-track.js reads the code from the path.
/offer-oct/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-nov/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-dec/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-jan/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-dec-countdown/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-feb/:code  /nsw  200
/offer-mar/:code  /nsw  200
/nsw/:code        /nsw  200
/gflam/:code      /nsw  200
/coaster/:code    /nsw  200
/home/:code       /     200
# /quick/:code: a tracked link to Play a quick game (INBOX 412 + 413, merged 15 Nov 2026)
/quick/:code      /quick  200

